goal:
satisfies_hash_partition() is variadic in its last argument. Passing VARIADIC NULL in place of a list of values crashes the backend.

    SELECT satisfies_hash_partition('mchash'::regclass, 4, 0, VARIADIC NULL::int[]);

It has to answer instead, and answer what the same call written without VARIADIC answers for all-NULL values, which is false. Calls with real values must keep returning what they return now, and the existing errors for a wrong number of arguments must stay.
